---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Site/Navigation';
import Footer from '../components/Site/Footer';
import { FlowIngress } from '../components/DocFlows/FlowIngressMinimal.jsx';
---

<Layout
  title="Data Privacy & Zero Retention | Inspectr"
  description="Inspectr Ingress securely forwards live API and webhook traffic without persistently storing proxied payloads on the ingress side."
  keywords="Inspectr data privacy, zero data retention, Inspectr Ingress, API privacy, webhook privacy, data minimization"
  ogTitle="Data Privacy & Zero Retention | Inspectr"
  ogDescription="Inspectr Ingress is a forwarding layer, not a data store. Understand how live traffic moves through Inspectr without persistent payload storage on the ingress side."
  canonical="https://inspectr.dev/data-privacy/"
>
  <Navigation client:load />

  <main class="bg-brand-dark text-white">
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-cyan-400/10">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_top_right,rgba(0,229,255,0.13),transparent_42%),radial-gradient(circle_at_bottom_left,rgba(0,184,212,0.09),transparent_38%)]"></div>
      <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-20 pt-36 sm:px-6 sm:pb-24 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <p class="mb-5 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-brand-primary">
            Data privacy &amp; zero retention
          </p>
          <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">
            <span class="block">Zero data retention,</span>
            <span class="text-gradient">by architecture.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-300 sm:text-xl">
            Inspectr Ingress forwards your API and webhook requests and responses to your environment. It does
            not store the payloads it relays.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-9 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
            <a
              href="#architecture"
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-primary px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-brand-dark transition-colors hover:bg-brand-secondary"
            >
              See how it works <span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2">↓</span>
            </a>
            <a
              href="/docs/getting-started/quick-start/"
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-cyan-300/30 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-brand-primary transition-colors hover:border-brand-primary hover:bg-cyan-400/10"
            >
              Start with Inspectr
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-16 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-cyan-300/20 bg-white/[0.04] p-5">
            <p class="text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-brand-primary">Real-time pass-through</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-300">Requests and responses move directly through Inspectr Ingress</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-cyan-300/20 bg-white/[0.04] p-5">
            <p class="text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-brand-primary">Processing in memory</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-300">Payloads are handled transiently during the live request</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-cyan-300/20 bg-white/[0.04] p-5">
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-primary">0 bytes</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-300">Retained on the Ingress side</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="architecture" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-primary">The architecture</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">A relay, not a data warehouse.</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-300">
          Public traffic enters through Inspectr Ingress, travels to your local Inspectr instance, and reaches
          your backend. The Ingress layer connects the outside world to your environment. It does not build
          a hosted copy of the traffic it forwards.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-cyan-300/20 bg-black/20 p-5 sm:p-8">
        <div class="grid items-center gap-4 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1.15fr_auto_1fr]">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-700 bg-gray-900/70 p-5 text-center">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500">Source</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 font-semibold">Client / webhook provider</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-400">Your users, apps, or third-party services</p>
          </div>

          <div class="hidden text-center text-2xl text-brand-primary lg:block" aria-hidden="true">→</div>

          <div class="rounded-xl border border-brand-primary/70 bg-brand-primary/[0.08] p-5 text-center shadow-[0_0_35px_rgba(0,229,255,0.12)]">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-primary">Pass-through only</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 font-semibold">Inspectr Ingress</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-300">Forwards requests and responses; no persistent payload storage</p>
          </div>

          <div class="hidden text-center text-2xl text-brand-primary lg:block" aria-hidden="true">→</div>

          <div class="rounded-xl border border-orange-300/40 bg-orange-300/[0.06] p-5 text-center">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-200">Your environment</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 font-semibold">Inspectr + backend</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-400">Inspection, history, replay, and application storage</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-center gap-3 text-center text-sm text-gray-400">
          <span class="h-px w-10 bg-gray-700"></span>
          <span>Relay processing is transient and non-persistent on the Ingress side.</span>
          <span class="h-px w-10 bg-gray-700"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-gray-800 bg-black/20 p-5 sm:p-8">
        <div class="mb-5 flex flex-col gap-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500">Inspectr flow</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold">The request path in practice</h3>
          </div>
          <a href="/docs/concepts/architecture/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-primary hover:underline">
            View architecture docs <span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-1">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <FlowIngress client:only="react" />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-brand-primary/30 bg-brand-primary/[0.05] p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-primary">Hosted layer</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold">Inspectr Ingress</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-300">
            Ingress is the public relay. It accepts the connection, forwards the request and response, and does
            not persist the proxied payload content.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-primary">Zero payload retention on the hosted relay</p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-orange-300/30 bg-orange-300/[0.04] p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-200">Local layer</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold">Inspectr Proxy</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-300">
            The local proxy receives the traffic and powers inspection, history, replay, and forwarding to your
            backend. Any operation history is held in your environment and follows your configuration.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-orange-200">Local retention under your control</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-4xl text-center text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400">
        In other words, zero data retention describes the hosted Ingress boundary. Inspectr’s local-first design
        keeps inspection data in the environment where you run it, so you decide whether operations are ephemeral
        or stored for later search and replay.
      </p>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-brand-primary/20 bg-brand-primary/[0.05] px-5 py-4 text-center text-sm leading-6 text-gray-300">
        <strong class="text-white">Ingress is optional.</strong> It is used only with the tunnel or
        <code class="rounded bg-black/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-brand-primary">--expose</code> option. Standard local
        traffic goes directly to your Inspectr Proxy and never passes through the hosted Ingress service.
      </div>

    </section>

    <section class="border-y border-cyan-400/10 bg-black/10">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-primary">What zero data retention gives you</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">No hosted payload store to secure.</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-gray-300">
            Inspectr Ingress has one job: move traffic between your public endpoint and your environment. It
            does not create a second hosted copy of the traffic, so sensitive payloads stay with the systems
            your team controls.
          </p>
          <a href="/docs/concepts/architecture/" class="mt-6 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold text-brand-primary hover:underline">
            Read the technical architecture <span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="rounded-xl border border-gray-800 bg-brand-dark/70 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold">Reduced exposure</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400">Ingress does not become a second long-lived home for your traffic.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rounded-xl border border-gray-800 bg-brand-dark/70 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold">Relay by design</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400">Ingress forwards the request and response between the public endpoint and your environment.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rounded-xl border border-gray-800 bg-brand-dark/70 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold">Clear ownership</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400">Local history and replay remain in the environment your team operates.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rounded-xl border border-gray-800 bg-brand-dark/70 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold">Data minimization</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400">The relay only needs to process the traffic required to deliver the live request.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-primary">Data handling</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Inspectr Ingress stores no payloads.</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-300">
          Inspectr Ingress forwards request and response content to your environment and releases it after the
          relay. It does not persist payloads. Any history or persistence happens in your Inspectr instance or
          downstream systems, where your team controls storage and retention.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-brand-primary/30 bg-brand-primary/[0.05] p-6 sm:p-8">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-primary">Ingress does not store</h3>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-gray-200">
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-primary">✓</span><span>Request bodies</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-primary">✓</span><span>Response bodies</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-primary">✓</span><span>Query parameters</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-primary">✓</span><span>Request and response headers</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-primary">✓</span><span>Proxied request/response payload content</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-800 bg-black/20 p-6 sm:p-8">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">The rest remains explicit</h3>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-5 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-300">
            <p><strong class="text-white">Local Inspectr:</strong> request history and replay can be stored locally under your control.</p>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Your application:</strong> data written to your own backend, database, warehouse, or downstream tools follows your policies.</p>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Operations:</strong> limited technical and security telemetry may be retained for reliability and abuse prevention.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="mt-7 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold text-brand-primary hover:underline">
            Read the Privacy Policy <span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2">→</span>
          </a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-y border-cyan-400/10 bg-black/10">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-primary">Privacy by architecture</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Inspectr Ingress forwards traffic. It does not store it.</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-300">
          <p>
            When a public request arrives at an Inspectr Ingress endpoint, the relay forwards it to your local
            Inspectr instance. Inspectr can then inspect, store, replay, or forward the operation according to
            the configuration in your environment.
          </p>
          <p>
            The hosted ingress layer does not retain the proxied request or response content after the live
            relay. That distinction keeps the third-party service boundary small while preserving the debugging
            workflow developers need.
          </p>
          <p>
            This works alongside transport encryption, access controls, and your own retention policies. It is
            not a replacement for them. Review the <a class="text-brand-primary hover:underline" href="/terms/">Terms</a>
            and <a class="text-brand-primary hover:underline" href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for the
            complete service boundaries.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-28">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-primary">Questions, answered</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Data privacy FAQ</h2>

      <div class="mt-10 divide-y divide-gray-800 rounded-2xl border border-gray-800 bg-black/20 px-6 sm:px-8">
        <details class="group py-6" open>
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-semibold marker:hidden">
            Does Inspectr store data sent through Ingress?
            <span class="text-2xl font-normal text-brand-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">No. Inspectr Ingress does not store request or response payloads sent through the relay. It forwards traffic to your Inspectr instance without creating a persistent hosted copy. Zero data retention is part of how Ingress is built, not an optional setting added after the fact. Your local Inspectr instance and your own application may store traffic according to your configuration and retention policies.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group py-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-semibold marker:hidden">
            Can I still use request history and replay?
            <span class="text-2xl font-normal text-brand-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">Yes. Inspectr’s local application can keep request history and support replay in your environment. That local storage is separate from the hosted Ingress relay.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group py-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-semibold marker:hidden">
            Does local traffic go through Inspectr Ingress?
            <span class="text-2xl font-normal text-brand-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">No. Local traffic goes directly to your Inspectr Proxy. Inspectr Ingress is involved only when you use the tunnel or <code class="rounded bg-gray-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-brand-primary">--expose</code> option to make a local service publicly reachable.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group py-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-semibold marker:hidden">
            Does zero retention include operational metadata?
            <span class="text-2xl font-normal text-brand-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">The zero-retention commitment is about proxied payload content. Limited technical and security telemetry may be processed for reliability and abuse prevention, as described in the <a class="text-brand-primary hover:underline" href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group py-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-semibold marker:hidden">
            How is this different from a proxy that caches traffic?
            <span class="text-2xl font-normal text-brand-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">A caching proxy keeps a copy and may serve later requests from that copy. Inspectr Ingress forwards the live request to your environment and does not create a persistent hosted copy of the proxied payload.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group py-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-semibold marker:hidden">
            Does Inspectr control data stored by my application?
            <span class="text-2xl font-normal text-brand-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">No. Once traffic reaches your Inspectr instance, backend, database, analytics tool, or another downstream service, its retention is governed by that environment’s configuration and policy.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-cyan-400/10">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-20 text-center sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Inspect traffic without creating another data store.</h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-300">
          See the full request path, keep control of local history, and expose your services with a relay built
          to pass traffic through.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="/docs/getting-started/quick-start/" class="rounded-lg bg-brand-primary px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-brand-dark transition-colors hover:bg-brand-secondary">Follow the Quick Start</a>
          <a href="/docs/concepts/performance-privacy/" class="rounded-lg border border-cyan-300/30 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-brand-primary transition-colors hover:border-brand-primary hover:bg-cyan-400/10">Read the technical notes</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
